
#######################################################################
#########################   Screen Recorder   #########################
#######################################################################


📌 Method 1 — Install from Ubuntu’s Official Repositories (Easiest)
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install simplescreenrecorder
    simplescreenrecorder

🧰 Method 2 — Install via PPA (Offers Latest Build)
    sudo add-apt-repository ppa:maarten-baert/simplescreenrecorder
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install simplescreenrecorder
    simplescreenrecorder

📦 Method 3 — Install via Snap (Sandboxed Package)
    sudo snap install simplescreenrecorder



#######################################################################
###########################   Screenshot   ############################
#######################################################################

✅ Method 1 — Install from Official Repository (Recommended)
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install flameshot
    flameshot gui

🚀 Method 2 — Install via Snap
    sudo snap install flameshot
    flameshot


⚙️ Set Flameshot as Default Screenshot Tool (Optional)
        If you're using GNOME (default in Ubuntu 24.04):
            Open Settings → Keyboard → View and Customize Shortcuts
            Go to Custom Shortcuts
            Add a new shortcut:
                Name: Flameshot
                Command: flameshot gui

        Set shortcut to PrtSc (Print Screen)
        ⚠️ Wayland Users Note :
            Ubuntu 24.04 uses Wayland by default.
            If screenshot selection does not work:
                Log out
                Click the ⚙ icon on login screen
                Select Ubuntu on Xorg
                Flameshot works more reliably under X11.